    items: [
      { name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" },
      { name: "Resources", url: "https://arthavi.com/portfolio-tracker-without-gmail-access" }
    ]
  }}
>

    <main class="container" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);">
        <article class="prose fade-in" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">

            <h1>Best Portfolio Tracker Without Gmail Access (2026)</h1>

            <p style="font-size:1.15rem; color:var(--text-body); margin-bottom:2rem;">
                Many wealth tracking apps in India automate your updates by requesting read access to your Gmail account. While this is convenient, it poses a severe threat to your data privacy. A <strong>portfolio tracker without Gmail access</strong> ensures your personal conversations, OTPs, and private messages remain strictly private.
            </p>

            <h2>The Privacy Risks of Email Sync</h2>
            <p>
                When you click "Connect Gmail" on an investment tracking app, you are authorizing a third-party server to read your emails. Even if their API claims to filter only for "broker notes" or "mutual fund updates," the technical access granted is broad:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Read Access to All Emails:</strong> The system can scan your entire inbox.</li>
                <li><strong>OTP Security:</strong> Financial logins, bank OTPs, and password resets arrive in your email. Storing or scanning these creates a massive security surface.</li>
                <li><strong>Personal Data Profiling:</strong> Your salary slips, online shopping receipts, and utility bills are often read to build a financial advertisement profile.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Security experts advise against granting full email inbox permissions to transactional or analytics apps. It is far safer to track investments using files you manually provide.
            </p>

            <h2>How to Track Investments Without Gmail Sync</h2>
            <p>
                Arthavi provides a 100% secure alternative using <strong>local statement parsing</strong>. You get all the automation without sharing your inbox:
            </p>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Get Your CAS PDF:</strong> Once a month, download your official Consolidated Account Statement (CAS) from CAMS or KFintech. This SEBI-regulated statement contains all your mutual fund transactions.</li>
                <li><strong>Upload Locally:</strong> Upload the statement file into Arthavi. The parsing logic extracts your holdings directly in your browser. The file is never read by third-party advertisement networks.</li>
                <li><strong>Daily Auto-Updates:</strong> Once imported, Arthavi updates your fund values and stock prices daily using live AMFI and stock market data feeds.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Comparison: Gmail Reader vs. Local File Uploads</h2>

